# .NET
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
*.swp

# EF Core scaffolding artifacts (migrations are hand-authored; see scripts/ef-migrations-add.sh)
**/Migrations/*.Designer.cs
**/Migrations/*ModelSnapshot.cs

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Local env overrides (never commit secrets)
appsettings.Local.json
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.hc-dev-stack.state

# AI tooling (local only, per SETUP.md)
.codegraph/
.code-review-graph/
claude-mem/

# Transient DevOps thoughts (review, repro, research, goals, Push JSON).
# Never commit these. Moving them to finalized later does not remove
# blobs from already-pushed commits. Keepfile only.
# The whole subtree is ignored rather than the two known subdirectories, so a
# file dropped straight into .cursor/thoughts/ is covered too. The directory
# re-include is required: without it the .gitkeep negation cannot be reached.
.cursor/thoughts/**
!.cursor/thoughts/non-finalized/
!.cursor/thoughts/non-finalized/.gitkeep

# Reviewer / Security / QA scratch files. A probe that exercises the compiler
# or a linter has to sit inside a real project directory, so it cannot live
# under .cursor/thoughts/. These reserved names may appear anywhere and are
# never committed: reviewer, Security and QA process output does not belong on
# the submitted timeline.
#
# Write them lower-case. These patterns are case-sensitive on Linux and on CI,
# but core.ignorecase defaults to true on macOS and Windows, so `_Scratch/`
# would be silently ignored there and tracked here. scripts/check-clean-timeline.sh
# matches case-insensitively so any casing still fails the build rather than
# behaving differently per platform.
**/_scratch/
**/*.scratch.*
**/*.scratch

# Review write-ups. These are thought-process output and belong under
# .cursor/thoughts/non-finalized/, not in tracked history.
.cursor/reviews/

# Local CodeQL CLI databases and SARIF dumps
# `.codeql-db*/` rather than one line per language: a new language pack creates
# a directory this file has never heard of, and the point is that no CodeQL
# database is ever tracked.
.codeql-db*/
.codeql-db-csharp/
.codeql-db-javascript/
.codeql-db-javascript-typescript/
.codeql-db-rust/
# Any SARIF, not just codeql-*: a plain results.sarif is analysis output too,
# and the guard rejects the broader set.
*.sarif
# git's globs are case-sensitive on Linux, so `*.sarif` alone leaves `.SARIF`
# tracked on exactly the platform CI runs. check-clean-timeline.sh matches
# case-insensitively; this keeps the ignore rules from being the weaker half.
*.SARIF
*.Sarif

# Rust
rust/target/
backend/HomeworkCentral.Api/native/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local postgres volume password (generated by dev scripts)
.postgres-volume-password
